s that operated from January 1970 to 1981. (For the record company and full background/history, please see [l=Shelter Recording Company Inc.]) Russell would later found [l=Paradise Records (8)] in 1976.\r\n\r\nShelter label appearance:\r\n• When it began in 1970, the Shelter label was red, with an egg image bearing an inverted Superman logo*.\r\n(*From mid-1972 to 1973 [the remainder of Shelter's distribution by Capitol], this part of the Shelter logo was usually overstamped [obscured] with a black rectangle in response to a copyright infringement lawsuit and later settlement with DC Comics.)\r\n• After MCA took over distribution in 1974, the Shelter label was an \"S\" in egg-shape circle on orange tint background, with \"Shelter\" in curved black text at top.\r\n• The ABC-distributed Shelter label later became orange, with \"Shelter\" in dark orange print seen in a straight line at top.\r\n• In 1978, Shelter employed the eerie orange-and-yellow tinted \"Saturn & Moon\" design (the \"S\" egg now has a Saturn ring over it), which was later continued into the MCA era when it acquired ABC Records in 1979.\r\n\r\nLabel Code: LC 1766","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:44717","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":878,"name":"MCA Records"},"sublabels":[{"id":547338,"name":"Shelter Records, Inc."}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/44717-Shelter-Records","type":"label","urls":["https://bsnpubs.com/abc/shelter.html","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shelter_Records"]}},"/api/discogs/release/1103733":{"cached":true,"release":{"artists":[{"id":null,"name":"Everything But The Girl"}],"formats":[],"genres":["Electronic"],"id":"1103733","images":[],"labels":[{"catno":"5426162","id":750,"name":"Virgin"},{"catno":"7243 5 42616 26","id":9626,"name":"Blanco Y Negro"},{"catno":"Cdv 2966","id":750,"name":"Virgin"}],"styles":["House","Downtempo","Deep House"],"title":"Like The Deserts Miss The Rain","tracklist":["My Head Is My Only House Unless It Rains","Rol